voc.txt and output.txt
----------------------

voc.txt lists the 31,497 Cyrillic words that occur at least three times in
8,370 passages of Kazakh Wikipedia (kk.wikipedia.org), taken from the
`wikimedia/wikipedia` dataset.  Wikipedia text is available under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 licence and the GNU Free
Documentation License; a word-frequency list extracted from it is offered
here under CC BY-SA 3.0 with attribution to the Wikipedia contributors.
output.txt is the output of kazakh.sbl on voc.txt and carries the same
terms.  Both files are regenerated by make_voc.py.

The news corpus used to tune the algorithm is copyrighted and was not used
for these word lists.

Open question for the Snowball maintainers: CONTRIBUTING.rst asks for word
lists under an OSI-approved licence, and CC BY-SA is not one, but the same
document points to the `wikipedia-most-common-words` script as the
recommended way to produce a list, so Wikipedia-derived lists appear to be
accepted in practice.  If not, the list must be rebuilt from a public-domain
or OSI-licensed Kazakh text collection.
